I have absolutely no skills in Nethack --- I'm probably the worst
player out there. Take my just-finished game, for example. (Finished,
for me, always means killed by something silly.) I started out as a
Wiz-Hum-Mal-Neu with very good items -- two scrolls of enchant weapon,
a ring of slow digestion, a ring of polymorph control, and a magic
marker (0:99). There were two consecutive shops, all with great scrolls
and items, and just lying around in the dungeon was an uncursed ammy of
reflection (!!!!!!), uncursed elven boots, an uncursed helm of
brilliance, and a blessed +1 cloak of displacement. I also picked up,
off the ground, two uncursed scrolls of genocide.
     So I went on, going down a few levels of the Gnomish Mines, but as
most of my characters died there, I wimped out before minetown and went
through the regular dungeon. At dungeon level 4, I think, I was blinded
by a yellow light despite having a towel in my inventory, and was
attacked by something biting. Turns out it was a pair of wolves.
DYWYPI? Actually, no, I survived that with a few luckily aimed shots of
force bolt. The next pair of wolves that turned up were also slain. So
I go down and up a bit, and pick up a + of remove curse, which I didn't
manage to have any use for. I quaffed my two potions of gain level at
XL8 in fear that it would be destroyed later on, and also my ! of gain
ability. I also had poison resistance from a giant beetle, fearing the
poisoned attacks that might kill me. So far, it was looking to be one
of my best games ever.
     At DL 6, I ran into a single leocrotta that took out over half of
my 60 or so hp in one hit. I had nothing to fight back with, and
fearing that it would kill me the next hit, I genocided leocrottas.
Fine, I could always write more ? of genocide. Going down to the oracle
level, I picked up a pony and brought down my large cat from the level
above. I started digging out the oracle's square, when in came 3
soldier ants, which almost killed me before I genocided them as well.
Very well, that was a good choice for genociding anyway. So I went to
the room adjacent with the g- command, and ran into a sasquatch and
something invisible, which practically killed me in one hit. Prayer
restored my hp, and seeing as the staircase was but 2 steps away, I
moved towards it....
     The tombstone read:

Rest In Pieces
wowthisguyowns the Wizard
Killed by an invisible stalker, DL 7
Died with the best stuff you can have
At experience level ten to something
That even a level three wouldn't fear.
